2607.15632v1 | Both directions of Fuglede's conjecture fail in dimension two | Tao Zhang 
      Fuglede's conjecture asserts that a measurable set of positive and finite measure is spectral if and only if it tiles Euclidean space by translations. Counterexamples are known in every dimension $d\ge3$, whereas the one- and two-dimensional cases have remained unresolved. We construct two explicit $60$-point subsets of the rank-two finite Abelian group $\Z_{60}\times\Z_{12}$: one is a translational tile with no spectrum, and the other is spectral but does not tile. A finite-to-infinite transference principle lifts them to bounded subsets of $\R^2$ that are finite unions of unit squares. Consequently, both implications in Fuglede's conjecture fail in dimension two.
2610.17662v1 | Zero divisors in group algebras of torsion-free groups in odd characteristic | S. V. Ivanov 
      A recent preprint constructs a finitely presented torsion-free group $G$ with a finite two-dimensional classifying space such that $\mathbb F_2[G]$ contains nonzero zero divisors. We extend this to every odd prime $p$: there is a finitely presented torsion-free group $G_p$, again with a finite two-dimensional classifying space, such that $\mathbb F_p[G_p]$ contains nonzero elements $α,β$ with $αβ=0$. Together with the case $p=2$, Kaplansky's zero-divisor conjecture therefore fails over every field of positive characteristic. The new ingredients are a signed version of the parity cancellation, made possible by a bipartite random model on one side; a type design built from the projective plane over $\mathbb F_{p^3}$ with $p$ additional letters, which makes every cross-intersection congruent to $1$ modulo $p$; and a squared-word decay estimate for this design, proved with an explicit test vector. The geometric part of the argument is taken from the characteristic-two construction. The characteristic-zero case remains open.
2610.37817v1 | The generalized Cartan-Hadamard conjecture | Marcos Agnoletto, Márcio Fabiano Da Silva, Stefano Nardulli, Reinaldo Resende 
      We establish the generalized Cartan-Hadamard conjecture, including rigidity in the equality case. As a corollary, we obtain that isoperimetric regions are bounded. We prove the conjecture for Alexandrov spaces with two sided curvature bounds as well. A sharp Michael-Simon-type inequality for hypersurfaces in these spaces is also shown.
